# Optional: copy this file to `assets/env/.env` (see mobile/.gitignore).
#
# Leave API_BASE_URL unset to use platform defaults from `api_config.dart`:
#   iOS Simulator / macOS  → http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1
#   Android emulator       → http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/v1
#
# Physical device on Wi‑Fi — set explicitly (your Mac’s LAN IP):
# API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.234:3000/api/v1

# Google Maps keys are NOT read from this file — copy the example secrets files:
#   iOS:     cp ios/Runner/Secrets.xcconfig.example ios/Runner/Secrets.xcconfig
#   Android: cp android/secrets.properties.example android/secrets.properties
# Then paste your API keys (Maps SDK for iOS / Android enabled in Google Cloud).
#
# Google Cloud Console (same or separate key from GOOGLE_DIRECTIONS_API_KEY on the backend):
#   1. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Maps SDK for iOS" and "Maps SDK for Android"
#   2. Credentials → API key → paste into Info.plist / AndroidManifest.xml
#   3. If the map is beige/blank with no streets: key missing, wrong SDK enabled, or
#      API restrictions block the app (use iOS bundle ID / Android package for dev).
#   4. After changing the key: stop the app and run `flutter run` (not hot reload).
